From: fivefold3 <332818675+fivefold3.noreply.github.com>
Subject: wifi: ath12k: do not drop the whole fw stats event for a vdev with no peer

The per-chain RSSI stats the firmware returns cover every vdev on the pdev,
not just the one the request named. ath12k_wmi_tlv_rssi_chain_parse() looks
up a link sta whose address equals the vdev's BSSID, which by definition
only exists for a station vdev: an AP vdev's BSSID is its own address, so
there is never a peer with it.

For an AP vdev the lookup therefore fails and the parser returns -EPROTO.
That aborts the TLV iteration for the entire event, so
ath12k_update_stats_event() takes its error path and signals neither
fw_stats_complete nor fw_stats_done. Every caller of
ath12k_mac_get_fw_stats() then waits out its full one second timeout while
holding ah->hw_mutex, which serialises every other stats user behind it.

Running an AP and a client on one radio is enough to trigger it: each
station-statistics query from userspace (a LuCI status poll, iwinfo, iw)
blocks a second in D state and the log fills with

  not found link sta with bssid ... for rssi chain
  failed to pull fw stats: -71
  time out while waiting for get fw stats

ath11k had the same bug and fixed it in "ath11k: fix warning of not found
station for bssid in message" (2022) - its parser logs at debug level and
leaves ret at 0, which is what this tree's ath11k carries today. Do the
same here.

The vdev stats path a few hundred lines up already skips the entry; it only
warns about it, once per poll per AP vdev. Demote that one to a debug
message too, for the same reason: it is an expected condition, not a fault.

The stats_id assignment moves ahead of the lookups for the same reason it
sits there in ath11k - when no entry in the array has a peer, the id must
still be set, or ath12k_update_stats_event() falls through to the vdev/bcn
path, leaves fw_stats_done unsignalled and the caller waits three seconds
more.

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/wmi.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/wmi.c
@@ -8443,9 +8443,9 @@
 					   "wmi stats vdev id %d snr %d\n",
 					   src->vdev_id, src->beacon_snr);
 			} else {
-				ath12k_warn(ab,
-					    "not found link sta with bssid %pM for vdev stat\n",
-					    arvif->bssid);
+				ath12k_dbg(ab, ATH12K_DBG_WMI,
+					   "not found link sta with bssid %pM for vdev stat\n",
+					   arvif->bssid);
 			}
 			spin_unlock_bh(&ab->base_lock);
 		}
@@ -8543,6 +8543,8 @@
 		return -EPROTO;
 	}
 
+	stats->stats_id = WMI_REQUEST_RSSI_PER_CHAIN_STAT;
+
 	arvif = ath12k_mac_get_arvif(ar, vdev_id);
 	if (!arvif) {
 		ath12k_warn(ab, "not found vif for vdev id %d\n", vdev_id);
@@ -8556,10 +8558,14 @@
 	guard(spinlock_bh)(&ab->base_lock);
 	arsta = ath12k_link_sta_find_by_addr(ab, arvif->bssid);
 	if (!arsta) {
-		ath12k_warn(ab,
-			    "not found link sta with bssid %pM for rssi chain\n",
-			    arvif->bssid);
-		return -EPROTO;
+		/* The event covers every vdev on the pdev, and an AP vdev's
+		 * BSSID is its own address - no peer ever carries it. Skip
+		 * the entry rather than discarding the whole event.
+		 */
+		ath12k_dbg(ab, ATH12K_DBG_WMI,
+			   "not found link sta with bssid %pM for rssi chain\n",
+			   arvif->bssid);
+		return 0;
 	}
 
 	BUILD_BUG_ON(ARRAY_SIZE(arsta->chain_signal) >
@@ -8568,8 +8574,6 @@
 	for (j = 0; j < ARRAY_SIZE(arsta->chain_signal); j++)
 		arsta->chain_signal[j] = le32_to_cpu(stats_rssi->rssi_avg_beacon[j]);
 
-	stats->stats_id = WMI_REQUEST_RSSI_PER_CHAIN_STAT;
-
 	return 0;
 }
 
